.TH CYAML_LIST_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_list_remove \- remove and free a list element by index
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_list_remove(cyaml seq, size_t index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the element at position index from the list node seq and
recursively frees it together with all of its descendants.  All
elements after index are shifted left by one position (O(n) in the
number of elements after index).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - element removed and freed.
ccol_invalid_args   - seq is NULL, seq is not CYAML_LIST, or index is
                      out of bounds.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_list_push (3),
.BR cyaml_list_get (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_remove (3)
